{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"IMPLEMENTED — commit 90f3380347 on branch fix/043f-84aa-infra (NOT pushed to Gerrit per instruction).\n\nSHAPE OF THE FIX: one idempotent documented path. `scripts/install-gerrit-hook.sh` +\n`make hooks` (which `make install` already calls), and the bare curl is removed from both\nAGENTS.md and CONTRIBUTING.md. Chosen over 'make the curl smarter' because `make hooks`\nalready owns the chained pre-commit/Gerrit arrangement and already VERIFIES the Change-Id\nchain survived — it only lacked the ability to INSTALL the stamper, so it warned and then\nhanded the user a curl. Folding the install in removes the second path entirely.\n\nThe script is:\n* cwd-independent — resolves `git rev-parse --git-common-dir` and absolutises it, so it\n  behaves identically from the main checkout, a subdirectory, or a linked worktree.\n* non-destructive — when a pre-commit wrapper owns the `commit-msg` slot it installs to\n  `commit-msg.legacy` (the slot pre-commit's migration chain runs), never over the wrapper.\n* idempotent — existing Change-Id stamping in either slot is a no-op exit 0. Required,\n  because `make hooks` runs on every `make install`.\n* loud on the unsafe case (AC4) — a `commit-msg` hook that is neither a pre-commit wrapper\n  nor a Change-Id stamper is REFUSED with a nonzero exit and a message, not overwritten.\n* payload-validating — refuses to install a fetched file that contains no Change-Id logic\n  (an HTML error page or a truncated download would otherwise become an executable hook).\n* offline-testable — `REBAR_GERRIT_HOOK_SOURCE` installs from a local file, which is how the\n  test suite exercises it hermetically.\n\nEVIDENCE, both directions:\n* RED (defect pinned): test_the_old_documented_path_targets_the_shared_precommit_slot proves\n  `git rev-parse --git-path hooks/commit-msg` from a LINKED worktree resolves to the MAIN\n  checkout's shared hook, and then performs that write to show the pre-commit wrapper is\n  destroyed. RED for the docs half was 3 real offenders: AGENTS.md:224, CONTRIBUTING.md:55,\n  CONTRIBUTING.md:426.\n* MUTATION (fix pinned): changing the installer's `target=\\$legacy` to `target=\\$wrapper`\n  makes 2 of 5 tests FAIL — 'the installer overwrote the shared pre-commit wrapper'. So the\n  tests discriminate the slot choice, not merely that a file appeared.\n* END-TO-END on the real host: `make hooks` from the worktree exits 0, prints\n  'Gerrit Change-Id stamping already installed (…/commit-msg.legacy, chained by pre-commit)',\n  and commit-msg.legacy's md5 is UNCHANGED (88bebbbf62ce56b94f4f4c7139edc845) before and\n  after. Both real commits on this branch were stamped through that chain.\n\nAUDIT of the other .claude/settings.json hook entries for the same relative-path defect\n(ticket c6f6 — NOT fixed here, as instructed): the project settings file has exactly ONE hook\nentry, PreToolUse/Bash -> 'scripts/hooks/serena_grep_reminder.py', and it IS relative, so it\nis the single instance of c6f6 in the project file. There is no .claude/settings.local.json.\nThe user-global ~/.claude/settings.json hooks ('rtk hook claude', 'terminal-notifier …') are\nPATH-resolved commands, not relative file paths, so they are not affected. Nothing in this\nchange touches that entry.\n\nINCIDENTAL OBSERVATION, not a regression and not fixed here: `pre-commit install` (which\n`make hooks` runs) re-templates the SHARED commit-msg/pre-commit wrappers with an absolute\nINSTALL_PYTHON pointing at whichever worktree's venv ran it last. Before this session's run\nthe shared wrapper pointed at /Users/joeoakhart/fix/b718-9ac2-caplog/.venv. It degrades\ngracefully (the wrapper falls back to `command -v pre-commit`), but it means `make hooks`\nis inherently host-wide for the wrapper too. Same shared-hooks-dir root as this ticket."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785727850931054001,"uuid":"14269e57-f15c-422d-a08f-0f9b42309e66"}